<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> clockwise about O is followed by the reflection in the line <m>y = x</m>.</p><p>(a) Write down the single matrix for the combined transformation.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Which single transformation is it?</p><div>[ the identity (no change) | reflection in the x-axis | reflection in the y-axis | reflection in the line y = x | reflection in the line y = −x | rotation of 90° anticlockwise about O | rotation of 180° about O | rotation of 90° clockwise about O ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The matrix of the rotation of <m>90^\circ</m> clockwise about O is <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; 1 \\ -1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}</m> and the matrix of the reflection in the line <m>y = x</m> is <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; 1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}</m>. The first transformation's matrix goes on the right:</p><p><m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; 1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; 1 \\ -1 &amp; 0 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m></p><p>(b) Read its columns: (1, 0) goes to <m>({-1},\,{0})</m> and (0, 1) goes to <m>({0},\,{1})</m>. This is the reflection in the y-axis.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>reflection in the y-axis</p></answer>
</stack-static>